<title>UK: Jersey bank deposits up 1.4 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Jersey bank deposits up 1.4 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank deposits on Jersey rose 1.4 percent in 1996 to 89.6 billion stg, although sharp movement in exchange rates caused by the strength of sterling saw desposits fall two billion stg in the final quarter, the  States of Jersey financial services department said.</p>
<p>It said sterling deposits grew 7.8 percent in the year to 28.9 billion stg, and foreign currency deposits fell 1.4 percent to 60.7 billion.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
